From 697a381c53edd767130ad6f40ee6f003e51bfb90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/63] sdhci, mmc: the SD and eMMC controllers of the NVIDIA
 Tegra 2

- a device tree attachment, with Tegra 2 support and controller quirks
- give the command line some time to become free; only end a transfer on
  an idle data line once it was busy
- keep DMA coherent with the CPU caches on ARM; gather the physical
  ranges of a request in one ADMA2 transfer
- mmc_bus: keep asking an MMC device for its operating conditions, give
  up on an SD card that does not become ready
- mmc_disk: check the EXT_CSD before taking the device size from it
- mmc_disk, gpt: never write the start of the Toshiba AC100 eMMC, which
  holds the boot configuration of the Tegra

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
